--+LIVE-RATIO CONTRACT
--+-------------------
--+1. Each distinct maximum-HP change starts from the live pre-change ratio:
--+       current HP / maximum HP
--+2. A historical domain lease cannot override that ratio.
--+3. Maximum changes that occur while the same correction is still pending remain
--+   one staged transition and carry the pending ratio.
--+4. Transition damage/healing after the snapshot is applied as a delta only when
--+   its source scale is identified.
-- 
-- ZERO-FRAME CONTRACT
-- -------------------
---1. A pending health transition whose observed current HP becomes zero is
---   classified as TemporaryZero before ratio, baseline, source domain,
---   last-observed sample, or stabilization state can advance.
---2. The last valid nonzero ratio is frozen.
---3. Repeated zero frames continue to hold that ratio.
---4. The first recovered nonzero frame is RecoveryBaseline. It establishes a
---   new source baseline but contributes no healing or damage delta.
---5. Only later nonzero movement contributes damage or healing.
---6. The runtime never writes current HP while the observed value is zero.
---   A persistent real death therefore times out/cancels instead of being revived.
---7. The native HUD normalization hook follows the same zero/recovery behavior,
---   so a transition-owned zero frame does not collapse the normalized bar.
