--## Zero-frame rule
--
--A zero-current-HP frame during a pending maximum-health transition cannot alter
--ratio, source domain, baseline, last valid sample or stabilization progress.
--The first recovered nonzero frame becomes a new baseline without being counted
--as healing. The runtime never writes health while observed current HP is zero,
--so a real death is not revived.
-+`NormalizeDiscoveredHudLanes=1` enables quest/additional lane normalization when
-+`NormalizeAllHudLanes=1` is also enabled.
- 
- ## Build
- 
--Open `HealthScale.sln` in Visual Studio and build `Release|x64`.
--The loader-compatible output remains `xinput_other.dll`.
--
--## Test
--
--The pure transition model can be tested with any C++20 compiler:
--
--```
--g++ -std=c++20 tests/native/health_transition_model_tests.cpp \
--  src/native/HealthScale.Runtime/src/health_transition_model.cpp \
--  -o health_transition_model_tests
--./health_transition_model_tests
--```
--
--## Maximum-change authority
--
--When a new maximum-health change is detected, HealthScale snapshots the live
--pre-change `current / maximum` ratio. Historical domain-lease ratios are logged
--for comparison but are not used as the starting percentage. The queue log now
--contains:
--
--```text
--ratio-source=live-pre-change prior-lease-ratio=...
--```
--
--This makes chained transformations and detransformations preserve the health
--percentage that actually existed immediately before each distinct change.
--
