+-## Live pre-change ratio rule
++A fixed, allocation-free registry records discovered quest/additional lanes and
++gives each one an independent HUD transition tracker.
+ 
+-Every distinct maximum-HP change now starts from the fighter's live percentage
+-immediately before the change:
++### Kaioken x20 cancellation
++
++Large detransformations can briefly expose current HP in the old scale after
++maximum HP has returned to base. The runtime now accepts bounded mixed-domain
++pairs and treats the first target-domain clamp/rebase as a baseline, not a new
++full-health ratio.
++
++## Core percentage contract
+ 
+ ```text
+-live ratio = current HP / maximum HP
+-corrected current HP = live ratio * new maximum HP
++preserved ratio = coherent current HP / coherent maximum HP
++corrected current HP = preserved ratio * stabilized new maximum HP
+ ```
+ 
+-A prior transformation/domain lease may still retain an older percentage for
+-late-write remapping, but it is never allowed to seed a later transformation,
+-detransformation, Super Soul activation, or other maximum-health alteration.
+-This prevents stale-ratio healing after normal damage between health changes.
+-
+-## Zero-frame rule
+-
+-A zero-current-HP frame during a pending maximum-health transition cannot alter
+-ratio, source domain, baseline, last valid sample or stabilization progress.
+-The first recovered nonzero frame becomes a new baseline without being counted
+-as healing. The runtime never writes health while observed current HP is zero,
+-so a real death is not revived.
++A target-domain rebase during a decrease never overwrites the held ratio.
